Let $n = k - 2$. Then,
\[\log_{10} (n + 1)! + \log_{10} n! + 2 = 2 \log_{10} (n + 1)!.\]
This is equivalent to
\[\log_{10} (n + 1)! = \log_{10} n! + 2.\]
Since $n$ is a positive integer, we have $n! < (n + 1)!$. Therefore,
\[\log_{10} (n + 1)! > \log_{10} n! + 1.\]
This is a contradiction. Therefore, there is no such $k$.
